class:: ShaderGraph
summary:: Validated linear multipass chain for SCShader
categories:: External>Graphics
related:: Guides/SCShader, Classes/Shader, Classes/ShaderTexture

description::
ShaderGraph validates and commits a sequence of live link::Classes/Shader:: resources to the renderer. Each pass renders into a renderer-owned ping-pong target, and the next pass samples that completed target; the terminal pass renders to the native window and stores the next feedback frame. Every Shader retains its own WGSL pipeline and code::amount:: uniform state, so two passes may use different source files and control values.

This first graph implementation is intentionally a connected acyclic linear chain: one code::\out:: to one code::\source:: input for each non-terminal pass. It rejects branches, missing nodes, ordinary cycles, node/server mismatches, duplicate inputs or outputs, and freed resources before it sends a graph change. An explicit code::connectFeedback:: edge may target only the terminal pass; it makes the prior completed chain output the following frame's first-pass source. General directed acyclic graphs, per-edge texture formats/dimensions, independent branch outputs, and arbitrary cyclic feedback nodes remain future work.

Relative to link::Classes/Shader:: alone, ShaderGraph changes the renderer from one selected fullscreen pipeline to a safe sequence of fullscreen passes. It is not a general node graph or a substitute for a GPU compositor.

classmethods::

method:: new

argument:: server
Ready ShaderServer shared by all graph nodes. Defaults to code::ShaderServer.default::.

instancemethods::

method:: add

argument:: shader
Live Shader on this graph's ShaderServer.

method:: remove

argument:: shader
Previously added Shader. Its normal and feedback edges are also removed.

method:: connect

argument:: from
Source Shader pass.

argument:: output
Must be code::\out::. Defaults to code::\out::.

argument:: to
Destination Shader pass.

argument:: input
Must be code::\source::. Defaults to code::\source::.

method:: connectFeedback

argument:: shader
Terminal Shader pass in an already connected chain.

argument:: amount
Finite prior-frame feedback mix from 0 through 1. Defaults to 0.98.

discussion::
Creates the graph's only currently supported feedback edge. It is applied through the renderer's prior-frame targets and therefore has the normal feedback warmup: the first frame reads the cleared black target.

method:: validate

returns::
The validated Shader array in render order. Throws before sending OSC if the graph is malformed.

method:: commit

returns::
The committed Shader array in render order.

discussion::
Sends the full validated pass sequence atomically to the renderer. The renderer retains the previously committed graph when it rejects an invalid resource ID.

method:: clear

discussion::
Removes all graph nodes and restores the renderer's normal selected-Shader display path.

method:: free

discussion::
Clears the renderer graph and marks this language graph unusable. It does not free node Shaders.

examples::

This example uses the packaged extension. Run one demo at a time and wait for setup to finish. It creates its own resources; no earlier example is required. See link::Guides/SCShader:: for the full walkthrough.

code::
(
var source = ShaderDef.filenameSymbol.asString.dirname.dirname +/+ "shaders/fullscreen.wgsl";
v = ShaderServer.new(\guideGraph);
v.waitForBoot { |server|
    d = ShaderDef(\guidePass, source);
    a = Shader(d, [\amount, 0.35], server);
    b = Shader(d, [\amount, 0.8], server);
    ~scShaderSetup = Routine({
        var deadline = Main.elapsedTime + 5;
        while({ (a.isRunning.not or: { b.isRunning.not })
            and: { Main.elapsedTime < deadline } }, { 0.01.wait });
        if(a.isRunning.not or: { b.isRunning.not }) {
            Error("Both graph shaders must become ready.").throw;
        };
        g = ShaderGraph(server);
        g.add(a).connect(a, \out, b, \source);
        g.commit;
    }).play(SystemClock);
};
)
::

Cleanup before starting another example; wait for any renderer window to close:

code::
(
~scShaderSetup.tryPerform(\stop);
g.tryPerform(\free);
a.tryPerform(\free); b.tryPerform(\free);
d.tryPerform(\free); v.free;
)
::

